## 1. Introduction
Metal–organic frameworks (MOFs) are nanoporous crystalline materials whose structure is constituted by a tridimensional array of metal ions or metal clusters connected by rigid bi- or multipodal organic linkers (Scheme 1).1–5 Porosity, crystallinity and
